# Game end at the time limit (GAME-09, docs/m6-plan.md M6.1). Once time is up, the game ends with
# the action under way then, or at the end of the phase if none was (Tournament Rules 3.1.1), and
# everyone still in it gains half a VP (3.7.2). The winner has the most VP alone, ousted or not; a
# game win also needs 2 VP (zero-vtes rules-qa 6.9).
seed 14
timelimit 10m
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *8
library A "Iron Ward" *20
crypt B "Tomas Grey" *8
library B "Signal Fire" *20
crypt C "Ilse Várga" *8
library C "Quick Feed" *20
start
present A yes
present B yes
present C yes

# Alice scored a VP earlier (a judge's correction stands in for an oust here).
judge> vp +1 A
expect vp A 1

# Time runs out in Alice's unlock phase, with no action under way: the phase is the last.
wait 10m
expect timeup yes
expect status active
A> next
expect status finished
expect ended time-limit
expect vp A 1.5
expect vp B 0.5
expect vp C 0.5
# Alice has the most VP, but under 2: she wins, without a game win.
expect winner A
expect gamewin none
log public Game over. Time is up: everyone still in the game gains ½ VP. A wins
# A finished game takes no more commands.
reject:wrong-status B> next
